Answers 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 each have more than three A or B lines. Each line above was kept only where dropping it removes a clause the answer states: the timetable, the French ceiling, refinery coordination, the export pledge, and the 325 million tally are five clauses of what happened; the pump price, the March price, the people Bessent named, EU supply, and US distillate stocks are five clauses of why it matters; the president's diesel post, the Journal lede, the 50-and-50 proposal, the 20-day diesel demand, and the 426 million workbook are five ways of miscounting the agreement; crude-versus-products, Hormuz not restored, Hormuz volumes rising, and Wright's tight-diesel remark are the mechanism, with the September report adding the size of the lost flow; the March 400, the March ceiling, the US 172, the 133 million awarded, the open 40 million, Europe's fraction, Germany's reserve, Germany's "no further release," the September 30 threat, the spokeswoman's rejection, the president's refusal, and the sixth collective action are separate clauses of what changed.

## Sections

| Section | Question it answers (from answer 7, or 1, 3, 4, 5 for the core) |
|---|---|
| Kicker, headline, dek, reading modes | What changed, in one scan? The headline is answer 1 and still true after answer 3. |
| In this story (`story-toc`) | In what order will the five questions be answered? |
| KPI strip | What are the October figures, and which March figure must not be added to them as if it were a second pile? |
| What happened (`what-happened`) | What did the G7 agree to release, and what did the text not count? Also answers 1, 4 and 5. The mechanism stays in these paragraphs. |
| The catch (`the-catch`) | Is the 100 million new oil, and is it a counted diesel release? Answer 3. |
| Where this sits (`where-this-sits`) | How big is this against the March release and against the diesel price a stranger pays? |
| The export ban (`export-ban`) | What happened to the US threat to ban diesel exports? |
| What happened next (`what-happened-next`) | What is only scheduled, and who answered the same day? |
