src/pages/events/fuel-reserves/2026-10-02-g7-releases-100-million-barrels.astro:62:        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="1">On October 2, 2026, the leaders of the G7 countries agreed to release 100 million barrels of oil over four months, coordinated through the International Energy Agency, to begin immediately. Their statement promises a substantial diesel release within the first 20 days and gives no number for it. It sets that release "taking into account commitments that have already been fulfilled."<Cite s="govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02" passage="taking into account commitments that have already been fulfilled, we will implement our commitments with a coordinated release through the IEA of 100 million barrels (MB) to begin immediately over 4 months, including a frontloaded substantial diesel release within the first 20 days" /></p>
src/pages/events/fuel-reserves/2026-10-02-g7-releases-100-million-barrels.astro:108:              <h3>A massive amount of diesel, and no number for it</h3>
src/pages/events/fuel-reserves/2026-10-02-g7-releases-100-million-barrels.astro:143:          <p>U.S. stocks of distillate fuel oil were {distillate.sep25} thousand barrels in the week of September 25, down from {distillate.sep18} thousand the week before.<Cite s="eia-distillate-2026-10-03" passage="Stocks of Distillate Fuel Oil" /><Cite s="eia-distillate-2026-10-03" passage="(Thousand Barrels)" /><Cite s="eia-distillate-2026-10-03" passage="08/21/26 08/28/26 09/04/26 09/11/26 09/18/26 09/25/26 View History U.S. 103,391 104,187 106,274 107,859 107,431 105,180" /></p>
