11:1. Financing behind packages: Energy Department March 11 release and September 29 exchange request, plus the German energy FAQ. Admitted. The March statement says replacement barrels at no cost to the taxpayer; the September request says a 25 percent premium and more than $3 billion. No appropriation, budget line, or signed contract for the October 6 bids was found on those pages.
17:7. Announcement state: the October 2 text is an agreement to release, beginning immediately, with a report due before 20 days and a further meeting on more diesel. The September 29 exchange is a solicitation. Neither page says the October volume has been delivered.
18:8. Policy lineage: March 11 commitment, September 16 House bills H.R. 10422 and H.R. 10423, September 29 exchange, September 30 CNBC account of the president still considering a ban, October 1 Treasury post. Admitted.
23:13. Ground-level actors: Bessent's post names farmers, truckers, and businesses. The German FAQ is the member government's own page. No separate union or trucker filing was admitted.
